Subject: [PATCH] Apple embedded export: report missing ETC2/ASTC import instead of failing silently

Upstream bug: has_valid_project_configuration() sets valid=false when
rendering/textures/vram_compression/import_etc2_astc is disabled, but
appends NO error text — export dies with an empty "configuration errors:"
list. Cost us a CI debugging session (build-ipa2 run #1).

--- a/editor/export/editor_export_platform_apple_embedded.cpp
+++ b/editor/export/editor_export_platform_apple_embedded.cpp
@@ -2313,6 +2313,7 @@ bool EditorExportPlatformAppleEmbedded::has_valid_project_configuration(const R
 	}
 
 	if (!ResourceImporterTextureSettings::should_import_etc2_astc()) {
+		err += TTR("ETC2/ASTC texture import must be enabled: set rendering/textures/vram_compression/import_etc2_astc=true in project settings.") + "\n";
 		valid = false;
 	}
 
